-- title:
--   A ̄ K-point occupying a local corner of H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a $2$-dimensional $k$-space with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ trivial on some finite-level subgroup) that is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\bar k$ has no proper nonzero stable subspace. Let $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S_{\min}$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ membership in $S_{\min}$ is equivalent to $\bar\rho$ being ramified at $q$ (some inertia element at some valuation subring over $q$ acting non-trivially), and for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N\neq 0$ satisfy: all prime divisors of $N$ lie in $S$; $p^2\nmid N$; every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$; a prime $q\neq p$ dividing $N$ but outside $S_{\min}$ has $q^2\mid N$; no cube of a prime divides $N$; and the weight-$2$ level-$N$ cusp forms with integral $q$-coefficients span the whole space over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta\colon\mathbb T=\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,N\,2\,S\to k$ be a ring homomorphism (the algebra being the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_q$, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. On $H^1=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(N,\top),\mathcal O)$ let the family $\mathrm{opFamily}$ of operators indexed by the generators $T_\ell$, $U_q$, $\langle d\rangle$ commute pairwise, let $\bar\theta$ assign an element of $k$ to each generator, with $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with the full list of maximal ideals, $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ exactly for $i\neq j$) of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}H^1$ generated by this family. Fix an index $i_0$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring at $i_0$ to $k$ sending the corner image of each generator's operator to its $\bar\theta$-value, and assume the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H^1$ consists of parabolic homomorphisms (vanishing on elements of trace square $4$). Finally let $M$ be a module over $T=\mathrm{heckeLocal}\,N\,S\,\mathcal O\,\theta$ and over $\mathcal O$ compatibly, together with an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e_M\colon M\to e_{i_0}H^1$ carrying the action of $\pi(T_\ell)$ to the Hecke operator $\mathrm{heckeT}$ at $\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$. Then there are an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\chi_0\colon T\to\bar K:=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}(\mathrm{FractionRing}\,\mathcal O)$ and a family $a_0\colon\mathbb N\to\bar K$ such that for every prime $q\mid N$: first, $a_0(q)$ is a root of some monic $R\in\mathcal O[X]$ whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ is $(X-\bar\theta(U_q))^{\deg R}$; and second, for every $M_g\neq0$ dividing $N$, every newform $g\in S_2(\Gamma_0(M_g))$ (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem away from the level occurs at no proper divisor of $M_g$), every ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,M_g\,2\,\emptyset$ to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ and $\chi_g(U_q)=a_q(g)$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\bar K$ with $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\chi_0(\pi(T_\ell))$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, the element $a_0(q)$ is a root of the local polynomial formed from $a_q:=\iota(\chi_g(U_q))$ if $q\mid M_g$ and $a_q:=\iota(\chi_g(T_q))$ otherwise and $e:=v_q(N)-v_q(M_g)$, namely $X-a_q$ when $e=0$ and $X^{e-1}(X^2-a_qX+c)$ otherwise, with $c=0$ if $q\mid M_g$ and $c=q$ if not.
--
--   This is the occupancy step in the computation of newform multiplicities in the cohomology of a modular curve: it produces a geometric point of the localised Hecke algebra, supported on a prescribed corner of $H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)$, whose $U_q$-parameters are residually $\bar\theta(U_q)$ and are simultaneously roots of the local polynomial at $q$ of every newform compatible with that point. It feeds the one-level multiplicity statement [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self).
